# 0083-play-stopped-is-not-a-paused-build.patch -- a stop that ends a BOOT-ONLY run (Play) before the boot is an interrupted Play, not a paused or cancelled build.
# Applies after 0082. UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR: compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below).
#
# WHY (target/agent-work/pl/REPORT-3.txt, H1 of the Rust chain): crates/ibuilder-pipeline boot.rs now returns 131 (RC_PAUSED) / 130 (RC_CANCELLED) from a boot-only run when a stop request
#   interrupts the shader library's rebuild before the boot ("[stop] stage 5 boot-only: a <pause|cancel> was asked for during stage 3 ...: the game is not booted"); a pause keeps the
#   boot-only request (a later Play continues the library, then boots), a cancel consumes it. The app took 130 / 131 as a BUILD's: StopEnding() called RecordPaused() (a paused-build record
#   under the run's label "boot-only (the framework is built and signed)": a "Paused" card, chip and Resume for a build that never was) or ApplyCancel() (a cancelled build's cleanup).
# WHAT: PlayStop (GameAppRedesign.cs, pure): a boot-only run's Paused / Cancelled outcome is StopEnd.PlayInterrupted; a build's stays BuildPaused / BuildCancelled (unchanged). StopBegin
#   records the run's kind (runBootOnly); StopEnding switches on PlayStop.Of; PlayInterrupted (GameAppRedesignUi.cs): no paused-build record, no cleanup, the StopMachine back to Idle
#   (CleanupDone + Forget: no Paused / Cancelled card, chip or Resume), the game stays Ready (its framework and stamp are untouched; 0065 already clears pythonRanThisProcess on 130 / 131, so
#   Play works again in this process), one log line, and the line "Play was stopped before the game started" ("; Play continues it" for a pause) in the game sheet's launch line and under
#   the carousel's buttons until the next Play. No notification (a stop by the person), no queue move (a Play is no queue item).
# VERIFIED (2026-11-21, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile (-t:Compile,
#   ios-arm64): 0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080. Host harness (harness83: PAD81;P82;P83 over this tree): 178 of 178 checks, 9 new (the table, the lines,
#   the REAL StopMachine taken through a boot-only 131 and 130 then PlayInterrupted's CleanupDone + Forget to Idle, the wiring, boot.rs's contract text); 6 of 6 mutations killed.
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran; no boot-only run was stopped on a phone (the app has no Pause / Cancel button for a Play: stoppable is false, so only another source of a stop request, such as the
#   system's task expiring, reaches it).
